class:: BFCC
summary:: Bark frequency cepstral coefficients
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/MFCC2

description::
Traunmuller (1990) Bark mapping: z(f) = 26.81 * f / (1960 + f) - 0.53, with f in Hz. MIR2 uses the uncorrected rational mapping over the selected range; no low/high Bark correction is silently applied. Source: link::https://doi.org/10.1121/1.399849::.

The pipeline is raw FFT magnitude/power, triangular bands in Hz, natural logarithm with a floor, then DCT-II. Coefficient c is sum(logBand[j] * cos(pi*(j+0.5)*c/numBands)). Orthonormal mode multiplies c=0 by sqrt(1/numBands) and all other coefficients by sqrt(2/numBands). Optional liftering multiplies coefficient c by 1 + lifter/2 * sin(pi*c/lifter). This shares the DCT formula and normalization with MFCC2.

Silence has the finite logFloor-derived c0 and approximately zero higher coefficients; omitting c0 removes that constant term. All parameters except chain are initialization settings. Memory is 8*numBands*(fftSize/2+1) bytes plus work arrays; cost is O(numBands*fftSize + numCoeffs*numBands) per FFT frame. It adds no lookahead beyond the FFT. Narrow unresolved bands return logFloor before the DCT.

Like vanilla link::Classes/MFCC::, this turns a spectral envelope into cepstral coefficients; the Bark spacing and explicit spectrum, normalization, and c0 options make the representation different.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain whose buffer matches fftSize.
argument:: numCoeffs
Literal integer 1..64; cannot exceed the available DCT coefficients.
argument:: numBands
Literal integer 4..128. Default 40.
argument:: minFreq
Lowest filterbank edge, in Hz.
argument:: maxFreq
Highest filterbank edge in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.
argument:: include0
Literal 1 includes c0; 0 starts at c1 and requires numCoeffs less than numBands.
argument:: normalize
Positive divides each triangular filter by its sum of sampled weights; 0 uses sums.
argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 magnitude or 1 power. Default 1.
argument:: logFloor
Positive lower floor before natural log, default 1e-10.
argument:: dctNorm
Positive selects the orthonormal DCT; 0 uses the unnormalized sum.
argument:: lifter
Positive sinusoidal lifter length; 0 disables liftering.
argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two 256..8192, matching the FFT buffer.
returns::
numCoeffs control outputs in increasing coefficient order.

examples::
The first nonzero cepstral coefficient changes filter brightness; the next moves the filtered recording across the stereo field. This makes changing spectral shape audible.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot {
    Routine({
        var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
        s.sync;
        ~mir2Example = {
            var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
            // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
            var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
            var coefficients = BFCC.kr(chain, numCoeffs: 3, include0: 0, fftSize: 1024);
            var brightness = Lag.kr((coefficients[0] * 0.08).tanh * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.06);
            var position = Lag.kr((coefficients[1] * 0.1).tanh, 0.1);
            var shaped = RLPF.ar(source, brightness.linexp(0, 1, 250, 6000), 0.6);
            var fade = Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2);
            Pan2.ar(shaped * 0.18 * fade, position)
        }.play;
        ~mir2Example.onFree { buffer.free };
    }).play(AppClock);
};
)

// Stop and free the sample buffer.
(
~mir2Example.free;
)
::

